  "id": "dreamy-state",
  "term": "dreamy state",
  "definition": "In historical psychiatric writing, a dreamy state is a pre-epileptic mental condition marked by altered experience, often with hallucinations, illusions, or related false beliefs. It was described as a mixed, dreamlike disturbance that could come before a seizure and could shape actions carried out later in an automatic state.",
